        <p>Curated texts, sources, and further reading</p>
    </header>

    <div class="page-content">

        <div class="container narrow">
            <p class="canon-library-note">The primary sources of Arbora are ancient: Stoic philosophy, Buddhist suttas, the Tao Te Ching, Jewish wisdom literature, Sufi poetry, the Upanishads, Ecclesiastes, indigenous cosmologies. These traditions are the trunk. Contemporary nature writing and science appear later in this canon as companions — modern voices that reach toward the same truths.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="container">
            <div class="canon-grid">

                <a href="canon-philosophy.html" class="canon-card">
                    <h3>Classical Philosophy &amp; Sacred Texts</h3>
                    <p>The trunk — passages from ancient traditions that have been read and reread for millennia because they articulate truths about how to live that have not expired.</p>
                    <div class="canon-preview">The Stoics · Daoist Texts · Buddhist Suttas · Jewish Wisdom · Mystic Voices · Ancient Fragments</div>
                </a>

                <div class="canon-tradition-links">
